                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I guess I'm the canary down the well, being the first person to purchase and review the game instead of getting a free copy provided by the developer.\n\nI don't have much time on this game, because there's very little substance to the game. It's a practically mindless clickfest which has shades of both rhythm games and tower defense, but frustratingly manages to do neither one well. \n\nThere is no inherent rhythm to the game's dispensing of adventurers for you to skewer. While the game becomes easier if you manage to score multikills with the traps which allow multikills, it's far from impossible to just spam kills wherever you can get them and then make up for any you miss further down the line.... God knows the game provides many more traps than you need.\n\nSpeaking of the traps, the game resembles a Tower Defense, in that you must purchase defenses in order to utilize them. Unlike a good Tower Defense, you cannot choose either the location or type of trap: All the thought and ingenuity are taken from your hands by the developer, and the only thing you have to worry your pretty little head over is WHICH traps you'll pick first, which hardly matters.\n\nUltimately, the game is one of rote memorization and mindless repetition. It's very much NOT worth the sale price at 20% off, nor would I call it worth the full price.\n\nAvoid.",
